 # Features Guide
 
-Comprehensive guide to MeedyaDL's features. For troubleshooting, see [Troubleshooting](Troubleshooting).
+A tour of what MeedyaDL can do. For fixes, see [Troubleshooting](Troubleshooting). The in-app Help has the full detail for each setting.
 
----
-
-## Companion Downloads
-
-MeedyaDL can automatically download additional format versions alongside your primary audio download. This is configured in **Settings > Quality > Companion Downloads**.
+MeedyaDL downloads from **Apple Music**: songs, albums, playlists, artist pages, music videos and your personal library. Other services are planned but are not available yet.
 
-### Audio Codec Companions
-
-Six companion modes are available:
-
-| Mode | Behaviour |
-|------|-----------|
-| **Disabled** | No companions. Only the primary format is downloaded. |
-| **Atmos → Lossless** (default) | When downloading Dolby Atmos, also downloads ALAC (lossless). |
-| **Atmos → Lossless + Lossy** | Atmos → ALAC + AAC; ALAC → AAC. Maximum compatibility. |
-| **Specialist → Lossy** | Atmos or ALAC → AAC companion for universal playback. |
-| **Atmos → All Formats** | Atmos → AC3 (Dolby Digital) + ALAC + AAC. 4 files per track. |
-| **Custom** | Pick exactly which codecs to download via multi-select checkboxes. |
+---
 
-**File naming:** Specialist formats get a suffix (e.g., `[Dolby Atmos]`, `[Lossless]`, `[Dolby Digital]`). The most universally compatible companion uses a clean filename.
+## Quality and Fallback
 
-**Progress tracking:** Companion downloads stream their output in real time to the Activity Log and progress bar. The queue-level bar advances after the primary download completes (partial credit), while the per-item bar shows companion speed/ETA. Processing labels show the current activity (e.g., "Companion: ALAC 14/28").
+**Audio.** Pick the format you want, such as Lossless (ALAC), Dolby Atmos or AAC. If a format is not offered for a track, MeedyaDL tries the next one on your fallback list. The default order is:
 
-### Music Video Companions
+> ALAC, then Atmos, then AC3, then AAC Binaural, then AAC, then AAC Legacy
 
-When enabled, MeedyaDL automatically downloads the music video for each track (if one exists on Apple Music) alongside the audio files.
+Turn the fallback list on and reorder it in **Settings > Codec & Resolution**. You can also remove a format from the list and add it back later. The list can never be left empty.
 
-**Requirements:**
-- MusicKit credentials must be configured in **Settings > Cover Art > Animated Artwork** (Team ID, Key ID, private key)
-- Enable the toggle in **Settings > Quality > Video Quality > Music Video Companions**
+If only some tracks of an album come back in your chosen format, MeedyaDL fills the gaps with a more common format and leaves the files that already worked alone.
 
-**How it works:**
-1. After audio download completes, the app queries the Apple Music API for each track's music video relationship
-2. Tracks with music videos get a companion GAMDL download using your video quality settings
-3. Duplicate music videos (same video linked from multiple tracks) are automatically deduplicated
-4. Results are logged in the Activity Log
+**Video.** Resolution is a ceiling: you get the best the video has at or below your choice. The video format list (for example H.265 then H.264) is set in the same place.
 
-**Progress visibility:** Companion downloads stream their progress in real time — the global progress bar shows speed, ETA, and percentage during companion downloads. The queue item stays in "Processing" state until all companions and enrichment finish. Desktop notifications are deferred until all background work is complete.
+**Artist pages.** When you paste an artist link, choose which kinds of releases to get (main albums, singles and EPs, compilations, live albums, top songs, music videos). MeedyaDL also avoids downloading the same song twice across those choices.
 
 ---
 
-## Quality & Fallback Chain
-
-### Audio Fallback
-
-When the preferred audio codec is unavailable, MeedyaDL automatically tries the next codec in the fallback chain:
-
-> ALAC → Atmos → AC3 → AAC Binaural → AAC → AAC Legacy
-
-For GAMDL >= 2.9.1, the native `--song-codec-priority` flag passes the entire chain in one process. If that fails, MeedyaDL retries each codec individually as a safety net.
-
-### Video Quality
+## Extra-Format Copies
 
-Configure in **Settings > Quality > Video Quality**:
-- **Resolution:** 2160p (4K) → 240p, with automatic fallback to the next lower resolution
-- **Codec Priority:** H.265 (HEVC) and H.264 (AVC), reorderable
-- **Remux Format:** M4V, MP4, or MKV container
+**Companion Downloads** (in **Settings > Codec & Resolution**) give you more than one format of the same music in one go, for example a Dolby Atmos copy for good equipment and a lossless one that works everywhere.
 
-### Artist Auto-Select
+| Mode | What it does |
+| --- | --- |
+| **Disabled** | No extra copies. |
+| **Atmos to Lossless** (default) | A Dolby Atmos download also gets an ALAC copy. |
+| **Atmos to Lossless + Lossy; ALAC to Lossy** | Atmos also gets ALAC and AAC copies. An ALAC download also gets an AAC copy. |
+| **Specialist to Lossy** | Atmos or ALAC downloads also get an AAC copy. |
+| **Atmos to All Formats** | Atmos also gets AC3, ALAC and AAC copies. |
+| **Custom** | You tick exactly which formats you want. |
 
-When downloading from an artist URL, select which content types to include via multi-select checkboxes in **Settings > Quality**:
-- Main Albums, Compilation Albums, Live Albums, Singles & EPs, All Albums, Top Songs, Music Videos
+- Extra copies are made after the main download's lyrics and file names are finished.
+- **They never replace a file.** If a file with the same name is already there, that copy is skipped and the Activity page says so. Downloading an album again does not refresh extra copies already in the folder.
+- Each extra copy gets the same lyrics files as the main download.
+- Files get a short label such as `[Dolby Atmos]` or `[Lossless]` so copies can sit side by side. Standard AAC has no label.
 
-MeedyaDL creates a separate queue item for each selected content type.
+**Music video companions.** Optionally, MeedyaDL also fetches the music video for a track when Apple Music has one. This is in **Settings > Codec & Resolution > Video Quality** and needs your developer details (see the in-app Help, Animated Artwork).
 
 ---
 
-## Template Builder
+## Lyrics
 
-The Settings > Templates tab uses a visual chip/pill builder for creating file and folder naming templates. Instead of typing GAMDL format strings manually, you can:
+Configure in **Settings > Lyrics**.
 
-- **Click `+`** to add variables (Artist, Album, Track #, etc.) or separators (/, -, space)
-- **Click `×`** on any chip to remove it
-- **Toggle "Edit Raw"** for direct text editing (power users)
-- **See a live preview** with sample metadata below the template
-
-Available template variables: `{artist}`, `{album_artist}`, `{album}`, `{title}`, `{track:02d}`, `{disc}`, `{year}`, `{genre}`, `{playlist_artist}`, `{playlist_title}`.
+- **Word-by-word lyrics (Enhanced LRC)** are on by default. Where Apple Music has word-by-word timing, you get karaoke-style lyrics. Other songs get ordinary line-by-line lyrics. A **Test word-level lyrics connection** button checks it works for you.
+- The order is: word-by-word lyrics first, then the other lyric files made from them, then file renaming last.
+- **Extra-format copies get the same lyrics** as the main download, and a better set of lyrics found with an extra copy can improve the main file's lyrics.
+- **Lyrics format fallback** (on by default) tries other lyric formats when the first does not cover every track.
+- **Other formats:** WebVTT, Rich SRT (styled subtitles, on by default), ASS, subtitles embedded in the file, and the open Lyricsfile (`.lyrics`) format. Most are off by default.
 
 ---
 
-## Enhanced Lyrics (Word-by-Word Sync)
-
-When Enhanced LRC is enabled (default: on), MeedyaDL converts Apple Music's TTML lyrics to Enhanced LRC format with word-level synchronized timestamps.
+## Tags in Your Files
 
-**How it works:**
-1. GAMDL downloads TTML lyrics (forced as primary format when enhanced LRC is enabled)
-2. MeedyaDL parses the TTML XML, extracting `<span>` word timestamps
-3. Generates Enhanced LRC with inline `<mm:ss.xx>` word timing
-4. Saves as `.lrc` sidecar file AND embeds in the M4A/M4V metadata
+After a download, MeedyaDL adds extra information to your files, such as record label, copyright, release dates, advisory label and Apple Digital Master status.
 
-Songs without word-level timing gracefully fall back to standard line-level LRC.
+- **Last-updated date.** Files record the date Apple Music last updated the release, as it stood when you downloaded it. Library Scan uses this to tell when an album has changed.
+- **Apple Music IDs.** Files also record the album's Apple Music number (and the song's number), including earlier numbers if Apple Music changed them, so a release can still be recognised later.
+- **Album by album.** When one download covers several albums, each file is tagged from its own album.
+- **Explicit and Clean labels** are added to album folders and file names (on by default).
+- Optional extras: cover art saved with your chosen file name, a cover art upgrade from another catalogue (off by default), animated cover art, loudness (ReplayGain) tags, AcoustID fingerprinting, links to the same album on other music services (needs an access key), and MusicBrainz video discovery.
+- **Language lists.** Metadata language and the interface language lists show real language names, in a sensible order. The app runs in English; German and French translations are not complete yet, so they are only kept for people who chose them earlier.
 
-**Companion formats:** When Enhanced LRC is enabled, you can still select LRC and SRT as companion formats. TTML is locked as primary, but companions download alongside for maximum compatibility.
+---
 
-### Lyrics Format Fallback
+## Library Scan
 
-When the **Lyrics Format Fallback** toggle is enabled (default: on), MeedyaDL automatically retries with alternative formats if the primary lyrics format doesn't produce sidecar files for all tracks:
+The **Library** page looks through a folder of music you have already downloaded with MeedyaDL. For each album it shows whether songs or formats are missing, and whether Apple Music has updated the album since.
 
-- **Audio** (.m4a): TTML → LRC → SRT
-- **Video** (.m4v/.mp4): TTML → SRT → LRC
+Press **Re-download** on a row:
 
-Each fallback uses `--synced-lyrics-only` to avoid re-downloading media.
+- **Missing songs or formats:** only what is missing is fetched. Songs already in the folder are kept.
+- **Only "Content updated":** the album is downloaded again only if **Overwrite Existing Files** is on in **Settings > General > Preferences**.
+- If your files carry labels such as `[Explicit]` or `[Lossless]`, a re-download may add a second copy beside them, so MeedyaDL asks first.
 
 ---
 
-## Subtitle Formats
+## The Queue
 
-MeedyaDL can generate multiple subtitle/caption formats from the TTML source downloaded from Apple Music. Configure in **Settings > Lyrics**.
-
-| Format | Source | Styling | Setting | Default |
-|--------|--------|---------|---------|---------|
-| **Enhanced LRC** | TTML | Word-by-word sync timestamps | `enhanced_lrc` | On |
-| **WebVTT (.vtt)** | TTML/SRT/LRC | Plain text | `generate_webvtt` | Off |
-| **Rich SRT (.srt)** | TTML/WebVTT | Bold, italic, underline, colours | `generate_rich_srt` | On |
-| **ASS (.ass)** | TTML/WebVTT | Full styling + positioning + colours (BGR) | `generate_ass` | Off |
-| **Subtitle embedding** | SRT/WebVTT | Freeform atoms in MP4 container | `embed_subtitles` | Off |
-
-Rich SRT and ASS both support dual-source priority: TTML first (richest), then WebVTT. This enables future services (YouTube, BBC iPlayer) that provide WebVTT to produce styled output.
+- The queue is saved, so it survives closing the app. Waiting downloads resume on restart. Failed ones are kept so you can review and retry them.
+- Export the queue to a `.meedyadl` file and import it on another computer.
+- Albums that only partly downloaded can be retried for just the missing songs.
+- **After Queue Completes** can do nothing, open the folder, play a sound, close MeedyaDL, or restart, sleep or shut down the computer.
+- Before a download, MeedyaDL checks your internet connection and that the output folder can be written to. If you are offline, downloads wait in the queue and start when you are back online.
+- If a feature or service is ever paused for a while, the app shows a clear notice and it comes back by itself.
 
 ---
 
-## MusicBrainz Video Discovery
-
-When enabled (Settings > Quality), MeedyaDL uses the MusicBrainz database to discover music videos as a fallback when the Apple Music API returns no results. No credentials required.
+## Notifications
 
-**3-tier priority chain:**
-1. Apple Music URL search in MusicBrainz external links (highest fidelity)
-2. ISRC code search (standard recording identifier)
-3. AcoustID recording ID direct lookup (from fingerprinting)
+Messages always appear inside MeedyaDL. In **Settings > General > Notifications** you decide when your computer also shows them as system notifications:
 
-Also discovers cross-platform URLs (YouTube, Spotify, Deezer, Tidal, SoundCloud, Bandcamp) for future multi-service support.
+- **When:** by default, only while MeedyaDL is not in front or your pointer is on another screen. You can also choose another-screen only, or always.
+- **Which:** by default, only important messages (downloads finishing or failing, the queue finishing, a copied link, a shut-down warning, an update). You can widen this.
+- **Style:** in-app only, system and in-app (default), or system only.
+- Each kind of event has its own on/off switch. When several downloads finish close together, they are summed up in one notification.
 
 ---
 
-## Metadata Enrichment
+## Keyboard Shortcuts
 
-After each download, a 12-stage enrichment pipeline runs automatically:
+Use **Cmd** on a Mac and **Ctrl** on Windows and Linux.
 
-1. **Codec & source tags** + Apple Music API metadata (always-on) — 30+ freeform atoms per file including ISRC, UPC, genre, advisory, artist IDs, record label, copyright, release dates, Apple Digital Master, composer, editorial notes, duration, and more. Written in dual namespaces (`com.apple.iTunes` + `MeedyaMeta`) with industry-standard names (`LABEL`, `COPYRIGHT`, `COMPILATION`, `TOTALTRACKS`). Tag definitions driven by `tags.toml` — adding new tags requires only editing the TOML file.
-2. **Enhanced LRC** — TTML to word-by-word LRC conversion (opt-in, default on)
-2b. **Lyrics format fallback** — retries with LRC/SRT if TTML didn't cover all tracks (opt-in, default on)
-2c. **WebVTT generation** — converts TTML/SRT/LRC to .vtt (opt-in)
-2d. **Rich SRT generation** — TTML/WebVTT to styled SRT (opt-in, default on)
-2e. **Subtitle embedding** — embeds SRT/WebVTT in MP4 containers (opt-in)
-2f. **ASS generation** — TTML/WebVTT to styled ASS with colours and positioning (opt-in)
-3. **Animated artwork** — Motion cover art download via MusicKit API (opt-in)
-4. **AcoustID fingerprinting** — Audio fingerprint + MusicBrainz recording ID extraction (opt-in)
-5. **ReplayGain analysis** — EBU R128 loudness analysis via FFmpeg (opt-in)
-6. **Music video companions** — Apple Music API music video lookup and download (opt-in, requires MusicKit)
-6b. **MusicBrainz video discovery** — 3-tier fallback when Apple Music API has no results (opt-in)
-
-All enrichment steps use `spawn_blocking` for file I/O and `yield_now` between steps to prevent UI freezes on slow filesystems (FUSE mounts, cloud storage).
+| Shortcut | What it does |
+| --- | --- |
+| Cmd/Ctrl + D | Download page |
+| Cmd/Ctrl + J | Queue |
+| Cmd/Ctrl + L | Library |
+| Cmd/Ctrl + Y | History |
+| Cmd/Ctrl + K | Activity |
+| Cmd/Ctrl + , | Settings |
+| Cmd/Ctrl + Shift + . | Abort every active and waiting download (asks first) |
+| Cmd/Ctrl + Shift + ? | Show the list of shortcuts |
 
 ---
 
-## Queue Management
-
-### Persistence
-The download queue is saved to `queue.json` after every change. On restart:
-- Active/queued items are restored and resumed
-- Failed items are restored in Error state (not auto-retried) for manual review
-- Completed/cancelled items are cleared
+## GAMDL Versions
 
-### Export & Import
-- **Export:** File > Export Queue saves to a `.meedyadl` file via native save dialog
-- **Import:** File > Import Queue loads from a `.meedyadl` file, re-enqueues with local settings
+MeedyaDL uses a download tool called GAMDL. See your version in **Settings > Tools**.
 
-### Pre-Download Checks
-Before each download, two checks run:
-1. **Internet connectivity** — HTTP GET to apple.com. If offline, item is queued but auto-start is skipped
-2. **Cookie validation** — Checks if cookies are valid/present. Blocks download if expired (skipped for wrapper users)
+- **Recommended: 3.9.1.** This is the newest version MeedyaDL has tested.
+- **GAMDL 3.9.0 is refused** because it cannot download the AAC Legacy formats.
+- **GAMDL 4 is an optional, untested trial.** It is never installed unless you ask for it in **Settings > Tools > GAMDL Version Management**. Use **4.0.2** or newer: 4.0.0 and 4.0.1 are refused because of known problems. If anything goes wrong, go back to 3.9.1 and please report it. See the in-app Help, External Tools.
+- Windows on ARM and 32-bit ARM Linux stay on older versions that can be installed there.
 
 ---
 
 ## Crash Reporting
 
-### Local Reports
-- **Rust panics** → JSON crash reports in `{app_data_dir}/crashes/`
-- **Frontend errors** → Persisted via `log_frontend_error` IPC command
-- **Download errors** → Terminal failures saved as error reports (network errors excluded)
-- Reports older than 30 days auto-cleaned on startup
-
-### Logging
-- Dual output: stderr + daily-rotating log file in `{app_data_dir}/logs/`
-- Uses `tracing` ecosystem with `log` compatibility
-
-### Reporting to GitHub
-Settings > Advanced > Error Reporting lets you submit error reports to GitHub Issues with a pre-filled issue form (privacy preview before submission).
-
-### Sentry (Optional)
-Opt-in telemetry via Settings > Advanced > Sentry toggle (default: off).
+- Crash and error reports are saved on your own computer, and old ones are cleaned up automatically.
+- In **Settings > Advanced > Error Reporting** you can report a problem to GitHub. A pre-filled issue opens in your browser, and you see exactly what would be shared first.
+- Optional anonymous crash reporting is **off** until you switch it on. MeedyaDL asks once after setup, and you can change your answer in **Settings > Advanced**.
