-## How It Works Under the Hood
-
-- Long-lived channel branches are protected by two split rulesets in `.github/rulesets/`:
-  - `protected-stable-branches.json` — `main` / `release-candidate` / `beta` / `alpha` (no bypass actor, fast-forward only).
-  - `protected-cron-channels.json` — `nightly` / `weekly` / `monthly` (admin-bypass enabled so cron pushes can force-update them).
-- `auto-delete-merged-branches.yml` exempts the channel names from the standard PR-merge cleanup.
-- `release.yml` derives the `prerelease` flag from the tag suffix at runtime (`prerelease: contains(tag, '-')`).
-- The macOS codesign `--timestamp` wrapper (see DEV_NOTES.md) is included in `release.yml` to work around an upstream `tauri-macos-sign` issue. It can be removed once the upstream Tauri fix lands.
-- All builds bundle their own dependencies (Python, GAMDL, FFmpeg, etc.) so installers are zero-setup.
+The number after the channel name goes up with each build. You do not pick it.
 
-## Conserving GitHub Actions Minutes
+## Reporting Problems on a Pre-Release
 
-Do **not** put `[skip ci]` in commit messages unless explicitly requested — every push to `main` should run CI. If you need to manually re-run a workflow that didn't auto-fire (e.g., release-please was skipped because a previous `[skip ci]` propagated through a PR body), use the explicit `gh workflow run` commands listed above.
+Please include:
 
-## Troubleshooting
+- The exact version, as shown on the **About** page in Help (including the ending, for example `-alpha.56`).
+- Which **Update Channel** you chose.
+- The steps that cause the problem, and the relevant lines from the logs. **Settings > Advanced > Diagnostics** has an **Open folder** button that shows where the logs are.
 
-### Build fails with version format error
+## Common Questions
 
-The version must match `X.Y.Z` or `X.Y.Z-(alpha|beta|rc).N` (for the push channels) or `X.Y.Z-(nightly|weekly|monthly).YYYYMMDD` (for the cron channels). The release-counter and date-suffix logic is automated — manual `workflow_dispatch` calls inherit the same parser, so mistakes are caught fast.
+**I do not see the pre-release update.** You must choose a channel that includes it. Stable users never see Alpha, Beta or RC updates.
 
-### Builds succeed but no installers appear
-
-The GitHub Release object is created before per-platform builds finish. Wait ~15-20 min for all 6 jobs. If a job fails, re-run it from the Actions tab; transient flakes (especially Windows ARM64) are common.
-
-### macOS build fails at signing
-
-Ensure all 6 Apple signing secrets are configured. See [Required GitHub Secrets](https://github.com/MWBMPartners/MeedyaDL/blob/main/DEV_NOTES.md#required-github-secrets) in DEV_NOTES.md.
-
-### Users don't see the pre-release update
-
-Users must explicitly switch the **Update Channel** in Settings to a channel that includes the pre-release. Stable users will never see Alpha/Beta/RC/cron-channel updates — that's by design (the in-app updater filters by channel, with promotion).
-
-### Cron-channel branch is stuck
-
-The cron workflows force-reset their channel branch to `main` on every run, so a botched merge state self-heals on the next cron tick. To force a manual re-sync without waiting:
-
-```bash
-gh workflow run "Nightly Release" --ref main -f dry_run=true   # smoke-test only
-gh workflow run "Nightly Release" --ref main                   # real run
-```
+**Installers are missing from a new release.** Builds for all computers take a while to finish. Check again after a little time.
